  "question": {
    "text": "A rectangular wire loop with length <math><mi>a</mi></math> and width <math><mi>b</mi></math> lies in the <math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> -plane as shown. Within the loop, there is a time dependent magnetic field given by <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>c</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>.Here, <math><mi>c</mi></math> and <math><mi>ω</mi></math> are constants. The magnitude of emf induced in the loop as a function of time is<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/zqnsdabscutzpepcsbehqzkresrqxbfrztwddiibcbzjllgeeu.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" />",
